WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.202
Find teaching session recordings
This page brings together lectures linked to LMS modules. Choose a calendar view or browse the module directory to find a session.

2
00:00:08.202 --> 00:00:19.595
Choose a calendar view
Use the View buttons to switch between Day, Work week, Week and Month. Select Week to see teaching sessions across the selected week. The small calendar lets you choose a date.

3
00:00:19.595 --> 00:00:31.464
Search for a lecture
Enter part of a lecture title, module or programme name. Use the results to find the session you need quickly.

4
00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:51.255
Filter the recording library
Choose the programme and recording status beside the search box. All recordings includes every status. Open More filters to refine the cohort, group and module, or include draft programmes and archived modules.

5
00:00:51.255 --> 00:01:04.118
Open lecture details
Select a lecture in the calendar to open the details drawer on the right. Review the date, time, programme, module and week. Scroll inside the drawer to reach the transcript, attendance and teaching quality check.

6
00:01:04.118 --> 00:01:14.584
Play or download a recording
For a ready recording, use Play to watch the video or Download to save it. Files that are not ready display their current status.

7
00:01:14.584 --> 00:01:25.951
Review attendance
Open View attendance and saved files to check learner names, time in the session and attendance status. Download attendance sheet exports the register.

8
00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:38.435
Find transcripts and teaching quality checks
Open Transcript to access the available transcript tools. Use Open teaching quality check to start a review of the teaching session.

9
00:01:38.435 --> 00:01:48.864
Browse by LMS module
Select All LMS modules, then expand a module to see its weeks and recordings. This provides another way to locate a teaching session.

10
00:01:48.864 --> 00:01:57.494
Return to the calendar
Select Calendar to return to the date view. Find a session and review its recording and attendance before starting a quality check.
